The preceding sections define the deployed estimator and present its primary
comparative evidence.  The material below records historical coefficient-law
ablations and the optional full-state physical-error formulation.  These
studies are retained because they explain how the present design was reached
and where the reduced model is limited, but they are not required to understand
the deployed adaptation law.

